4{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -7\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3{b}_{1}-7{b}_{2} \\\\  & =-7{b}_{2}+3{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}(5{b}_{2})+\\frac{3}{4}(4{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-\\frac{7}{5}{c}_{1}+\\frac{3}{4}{c}_{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{7}{5} \\\\ \\frac{3}{4}\\end{aligned}].$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186432501 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119823 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "29b27833-e930-5339-89b3-c5651d791dcd" :knowledge-point/title "Writing a Two-Dimensional Vector in a Different Basis"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432476} {:answer/id #uuid "591225ac-bd90-5ecb-bd8a-ea3b808b5e20" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-4 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432479} {:answer/id #uuid "805154d8-bb48-5c28-8787-0a43308ed66d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-2 \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432483} {:answer/id #uuid "92932d78-c613-5c42-8f32-7950ba738ba0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2} \\\\ -4\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432485} {:answer/id #uuid "c63964c0-5683-5c24-a2a1-075e70846087" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}4 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}]" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186432489}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "50241126-2ee4-53c8-bb48-217fe294ace2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592