x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}].$ What are the coordinates of $x$ relative to the basis $C=\\{{c}_{1},{c}_{2},{c}_{3}\\},$ where ${c}_{1}=3{b}_{2}$, ${c}_{2}=-6{b}_{3}$ and ${c}_{3}=3{b}_{1}?$" :question/worked-solution "Since $[x]_{B}=[\\begin{aligned}15 \\\\ -24 \\\\ 18\\end{aligned}]$, we can write $x$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =15{b}_{1}-24{b}_{2}+18{b}_{3} \\\\  & =-24{b}_{2}+18{b}_{3}+15{b}_{1} \\\\  & =-8(3{b}_{2})-3(-6{b}_{3})+5(3{b}_{1}) \\\\  & =-8{c}_{1}-3{c}_{2}+5{c}_{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $[x]_{C}=[\\begin{aligned}-8 \\\\ -3 \\\\ 5\\end{aligned}].$"}]}
